1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:08,600
Five dental conditions. Five treatment stories. These
are simplified illustrations; treatment depends on
assessment.

2
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:11,600
Before the hole.

3
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:18,400
Early decay can weaken enamel before a hole forms. A
dentist checks the stage.

4
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:25,200
Fluoride and daily care can support mineral recovery.
This takes time and follow-up.

5
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:30,100
Early decay can recover. A cavity cannot simply grow
closed.

6
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:33,100
Repair the cavity.

7
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:39,900
Once a cavity forms, missing tooth structure may need a
filling after assessment.

8
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:46,700
The dentist removes damaged tissue and prepares the
tooth while preserving sound structure.

9
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:53,500
Tooth-colored composite is placed, hardened with light,
and shaped to restore the tooth.

10
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,000
A filling restores the defect. Prevention still matters.

11
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:01,000
Save the tooth.

12
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:07,800
Inflamed or infected pulp may need root canal treatment
to retain a restorable tooth.

13
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:15,100
Under anesthesia and isolation, the clinician removes
pulp, then cleans and disinfects the canal.

14
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:21,900
The cleaned canal is filled and sealed. The filling
material does not regenerate pulp.

15
00:01:22,400 --> 00:01:28,700
A final restoration protects the tooth; a crown is often
used when needed.

16
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:33,667
The tooth stays. The infected pulp is removed and the
space sealed.

17
00:01:34,167 --> 00:01:36,667
Below the gumline.

18
00:01:37,167 --> 00:01:44,367
Periodontitis affects tooth-supporting tissues. Deposits
can collect along roots below an inflamed gumline.

19
00:01:44,867 --> 00:01:51,667
Professional deep cleaning removes deposits along the
root surface. Treatment depends on disease severity.

20
00:01:52,167 --> 00:01:58,467
Inflammation can improve with treatment and daily care.
Lost bone does not instantly regrow.

21
00:01:58,967 --> 00:02:04,000
Control deposits and inflammation. Keep care and
reassessment ongoing.

22
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:07,000
Replace the missing tooth.

23
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:13,800
For a missing tooth, assessment checks bone and health.
An implant is one option.

24
00:02:14,300 --> 00:02:20,600
In suitable cases, an implant body is placed in a
prepared site in the jawbone.

25
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:27,400
Healing and bone integration can take several months or
longer. Success is not guaranteed.

26
00:02:27,900 --> 00:02:34,233
After healing, an abutment and crown restore the gap.
Cleaning and follow-up remain essential.

27
00:02:34,733 --> 00:02:39,500
An implant is one option. Healing takes months and
suitability varies.

28
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:47,633
These stories omit many clinical steps. A dental
professional assesses the condition and discusses
suitable options.
